Actually, monsters will only stone themselves when they attack
"barehanded", or with a bite, butt, swallow, etc...

If they attack with a weapon, they probably won't stone themselves,
unless they have other attacks that involve "touching".

You can still bite them yourself while in basilisk form.  You can also
lay eggs and use them as "stoning grenades" - but beware - each broken
egg that you laid yourself is -1 to luck.

Basilisks also make fine pets, although you may have trouble finding
enough to eat.

The Slashem spoilers at http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/
don't seem to include a list of resistances for monsters. Generally,
monsters are stoning resistant if they cause stoning, are acidic, are
stone/earth, or are incorporeal.



